%[text] %[text:anchor:T_5AB1737C] # Moments
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:MainMenu.m)
%[text] A moment of force is a measure of the amount and direction of rotation imparted to a system by a particular force. When describing a static system, it is required to track the balance of all moments. Vectors provide a helpful tool for such analysis.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] **Before you get started:**
%[text] This live script is intended to be used with the code visible and output inline. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB Toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Output inline**. Alternately, select **Output inline** using the icon ![live script output inline icon](text:image:138b) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
