%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D57DCAFB] ## Glossary
%[text] **moment:** The effect of a force that causes rotation. In physics, you may see this referred to as a torque.
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_4600CDDF] **Newton:** The SI unit of force, 1 Newton = 1 $\\frac{\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}}{\\text{s}^2}${"altText":"(kg dot m)\/(s^2)"}. 
%[text]     This is the force needed to accelerate one kilogram of mass at the rate of one meter per second squared in the direction of the applied force.  
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_7B183274] **resultant force:** The sum of all the forces in a system is the resultant force.
%[text] **unit vector:** A vector of length 1.
%%
